# 🔧 How It Works

## Step-by-Step Example: User "John"

### STEP 1: REGISTRATION

```text
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

John visits the registration page:
• Enters: Full Name: "John Doe"
• Enters: Phone: "9876543210"
• Clicks: "Generate Unique Key" → Gets: "Kx9mP2vL"
• Creates: Password: "MySecure@123"
• Creates: PIN: "5678"
• Clicks: "Create Account"

Backend:

Validates all inputs

Encrypts: password, PIN, phone, key (AES-256-CBC)

Creates MongoDB user document

Creates directory: /browser-profiles/user_{mongoId}/

Detects Chrome installation (background)

Returns success with unique key

Result: John's account created. Profile directory ready.
NO MinIO upload yet (waits for browser close).

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
```

### STEP 2: LOGIN

```text
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

John logs in:
• Enters: Unique Key: "Kx9mP2vL"
• Enters: Password: "MySecure@123"
• Enters: PIN: "5678"
• Clicks: "Sign In"

Backend:

Finds user by decrypting all unique keys

Verifies password (decrypt + compare)

Verifies PIN (decrypt + compare)

Checks MinIO for existing profile
→ First time: No profile in MinIO
→ Uses fresh local profile

Returns user data + chest items

Result: John sees congratulations page with his details.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
```

### STEP 3: LAUNCH BROWSER

```text
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

John clicks "Launch Browser":
• Playwright launches Chrome with his profile
• Chrome opens with all defaults
• John browses, logs into sites, saves bookmarks
• All data saved to: /browser-profiles/user_{mongoId}/

Backend:

Gets Chrome executable path

Launches persistent context with profile directory

Navigates to google.com

Registers 'close' event listener

Result: Chrome opens. John's browsing data saved locally.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
```

### STEP 4: CLOSE BROWSER (Auto-Upload)

```text
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

John closes Chrome:
• 'close' event fires
• 2-second debounce (ensures all files written)

Backend (Automatic):

Calculates profile size (e.g., 72 MB)

Compresses to ZIP (Level 9) → ~31 MB

Calculates SHA-256 checksum

Encrypts with AES-256-GCM (user-specific key)

Generates random MinIO path:
profiles/c7d44152/62e59299/v1/

Uploads chunk to MinIO

Saves metadata to MongoDB:
{
profileId: "uuid",
storagePath: "profiles/c7d44152/62e59299/v1",
chunkCount: 1,
checksum: "sha256...",
encryptionIV: "...",
authTag: "..."
}

Deletes local profile folder

Deletes old MinIO chunks (if any)

Marks cache as invalid

Result: Profile safely stored in cloud. Local cleaned up.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
```

### STEP 5: LOGIN AGAIN (Restore)

```text
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

John logs in next day:
• Same credentials

Backend:

Verifies credentials

Checks local cache → Invalid (deleted)

Checks MinIO → Found!

Downloads encrypted chunk (31 MB)

Decrypts with AES-256-GCM

Verifies SHA-256 checksum

Extracts ZIP → /browser-profiles/user_{mongoId}/

Updates local cache

Result: John's profile restored exactly as he left it!

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
```

