# 🔒 Security Architecture

## Encryption Pipeline

```text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ ENCRYPTION LAYERS                                                      │
│                                                                         │
│ Layer 1: TEXT ENCRYPTION (AES-256-CBC)                                 │
│ ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐      │
│ │ Passwords • PINs • Phone Numbers • Unique Keys • Profile Photos│      │
│ │ Format: {iv}:{encryptedData}                                   │      │
│ │ Key: SHA-256(MASTER_SECRET)                                    │      │
│ └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘      │
│                                                                         │
│ Layer 2: CHUNK ENCRYPTION (AES-256-GCM)                                │
│ ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐      │
│ │ Profile ZIP Chunks (50MB each)                                 │      │
│ │ Format: [IV(12)] + [AuthTag(16)] + [Encrypted Data]            │      │
│ │ Key: scrypt(MASTER_SECRET, "user-{userId}", 32)                │      │
│ │ Provides: Confidentiality + Integrity + Authenticity           │      │
│ └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘      │
│                                                                         │
│ Layer 3: TRANSPORT SECURITY                                            │
│ ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐      │
│ │ HTTPS (Production) • MinIO TLS • MongoDB TLS                   │      │
│ └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘      │
│                                                                         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Key Management

```text
MASTER_SECRET (Environment Variable)
│
├── SHA-256 → TEXT_ENCRYPTION_KEY (32 bytes)
│   Used for: AES-256-CBC (passwords, PINs, etc.)
│
└── scrypt(MASTER_SECRET, "user-{userId}") → USER_KEY (32 bytes)
    Used for: AES-256-GCM (profile chunks)
    Unique per user!
```

---

# 🚀 Installation

## Prerequisites

- **Node.js** 18.x or higher
- **MongoDB Atlas** account (or local MongoDB)
- **MinIO** server running locally or remotely
- **Google Chrome** installed
- **Git** installed

## Step 1: Clone Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/cloude.git
cd cloude
```

## Step 2: Install Backend Dependencies

```bash
cd backend
npm install
```

## Step 3: Configure Environment

```bash
# Copy example env file
cp .env.example .env

# Edit .env with your values
nano .env
```

### Required .env variables

```env
PORT=5000
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://<user>:<pass>@cluster.mongodb.net/cloude
MINIO_ENDPOINT=localhost
MINIO_PORT=9000
MINIO_ACCESS_KEY=admin
MINIO_SECRET_KEY=admin12345
MASTER_SECRET=your-64-char-random-secret-key
```

## Step 4: Install Frontend Dependencies

```bash
cd ../frontend
npm install
```

## Step 5: Start MinIO Server

```bash
# Using Docker
docker run -p 9000:9000 -p 9001:9001 \
  -e MINIO_ROOT_USER=admin \
  -e MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=admin12345 \
  quay.io/minio/minio server /data --console-address ":9001"

# Or download from https://min.io/download
```

## Step 6: Start Backend Server

```bash
cd backend
node server.js
```

## Step 7: Start Frontend

```bash
cd frontend
npm start
```

## Step 8: Access Application

Frontend: http://localhost:3000

Backend API: http://localhost:5000

MinIO Console: http://localhost:9001

